# XSH feclearexcept()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Every exception macro is optional (XBD <fenv.h>): a test that uses one is
# NOTINUSE when it is not defined. Exceptions are provoked by arithmetic on
# volatile operands.

assertion  XSH.feclearexcept.001
anchor     functions/feclearexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/feclearexcept.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       For each exception the implementation defines, feclearexcept() returns
           zero when it is called with that exception raised.
test       t/001-return.c

assertion  XSH.feclearexcept.002
anchor     functions/feclearexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       After feclearexcept() is given an exception that was raised,
           fetestexcept() reports that exception as not set.
test       t/002-cleared.c

assertion  XSH.feclearexcept.003
anchor     functions/feclearexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       Clearing one exception leaves another, independent exception that is
           raised still raised (only the exceptions named by the argument are
           cleared).
test       t/003-others-kept.c

assertion  XSH.feclearexcept.004
anchor     functions/feclearexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/feclearexcept.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       feclearexcept(0) returns zero and does not clear a raised exception.
test       t/004-zero.c

assertion  XSH.feclearexcept.005
anchor     functions/feclearexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/feclearexcept.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       feclearexcept(FE_ALL_EXCEPT) returns zero and clears every exception
           the implementation defines.
test       t/005-all.c

assertion  XSH.feclearexcept.006
anchor     functions/feclearexcept.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       Clearing an exception whose flag is already clear counts as success:
           feclearexcept() returns zero.
test       t/006-already-clear.c
